<title>PERU: Peru cotton society issues prices up to Dec 9.</title>
<headline>Peru cotton society issues prices up to Dec 9.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's private National Cotton Society issued on Tuesday new cotton prices, which will be in effect until December 9.</p>
<p>The list of prices, which vary according to type and quality, show no changes from those in effect during the last two weeks.</p>
<p>The prices are as follows:</p>
<p>-Tanguis seed (superior) - no price given.</p>
<p>-Pima seed (superior) - no price given.</p>
<p>-Mountain seed (superior) - no price given.</p>
<p>-Tanguis ginned (3 1/2 grade - 1.5/32 inches) - $87.50 a quintal.</p>
<p>-Pima ginnned (1 grade - 1.9/16 inches) - no price given.</p>
<p>-Mountain ginned (1 grade - 1 3/8 inches) - no price given.</p>
<p>One tonne is equivalent to 21.74 quintals.</p>
<p>-- Lima newsroom, 511-221-2134</p>
</text>
